{
  "id": "29987_sekigae",
  "headword": "{席替|せきが}え",
  "reading": "せきがえ",
  "romaji": "sekigae",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "changing seats; seat reassignment",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "changing seats; seat reassignment",
      "explanation": "The rearranging of who sits where, especially the periodic reassignment of pupils' desks in a school classroom. Composed of {席|せき} (seat) and {替|か}え (changing). Takes する."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29987_sekigae_ex1",
      "japanese": "{明日|あす}{席替|せきが}えがある。",
      "english": "We have a seat change tomorrow.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29987_sekigae_ex2",
      "japanese": "くじで{席替|せきが}えを{決|き}めた。",
      "english": "We decided the new seats by drawing lots.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29987_sekigae_ex3",
      "japanese": "{仲|なか}のいい{友達|ともだち}と{離|はな}れて、{席替|せきが}えでがっかりした。",
      "english": "I was disappointed by the seat change because it separated me from my close friend.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Strongly associated with school life, where seats are reshuffled every month or term, often by lottery.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {席替|せきが}えをする: to change seats\n- {席替|せきが}えがある: to have a seat change\n- くじで{席替|せきが}えを{決|き}める: to decide seats by drawing lots\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {模様替|もようが}え: rearranging furniture in a room, not people's seats\n- {配置|はいち}{換|が}え: reassignment of postings or placements, e.g. of staff",
